      READ THE DISTANCE BEFORE ANYTHING ELSE. §81 wrote its own
      refusal in advance: a membrane-to-threshold distance of MANY
      noise SD means neither facilitation nor noise can reach it,
      and the lead dies there with no creature spent.
      AND THAT REFUSAL FIRED, AND IT WAS WRONG. THE TABLE BELOW IS
      WHY: read it before acting on this one.

    §81 RE-SPECIFIED PRE-FLIGHT — THE EXCURSION DISTRIBUTION.
    PRINT ONLY, NOT A VERDICT, NOT AN ARM.

      `sd` is the per-neuron SD of v_ WITHIN kSdWBE, averaged over
      the module: total within-window variation, trend included.
      IT IS NOT A NOISE SD AND MUST NOT BE QUOTED AS ONE.
      `gap` is the mean threshold-minus-membrane over the same
      samples and `gap/sd` is the honest replacement for the last
      column of the table above.
      `closest` is the mean over neurons of the SMALLEST gap that
      neuron reached in the window; `min` is the smallest anywhere.
      The four band columns are the share of SCORED (neuron, tick)
      samples whose gap is under that fraction of the neuron's OWN
      LIVE threshold -- the genome's birth `threshold` is NOT the
      operating one and IP retunes it per neuron and per protocol.
      `fired` is the share DROPPED because the neuron spiked on that
      tick, and ITS DENOMINATOR IS THE OTHER ONE: scored plus
      dropped, because a share of the drops quoted against a base
      that excludes the drops is not a share of anything.

      EVERY COLUMN IS A LOWER BOUND ON THE EXCURSION. The kernel
      resets v_ to v_rest on the tick it crosses, so no sample taken
      after step() can hold a value at or above threshold: the top of
      the distribution is censored by the very mechanism in question.
      `fired` is how much of it was removed.

